Z||000000||PAUL88GT||11-18-1999||07:42 AM||||I have a crack in the windshield in my 88gt. It was there when a I bought the car last month.  I am thinking about buying a used windshield at the local boneyard.  Are all fiero windshields the same? Can I use one out of any year fiero in my 88gt? ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Phil||11-18-1999||09:15 AM||||yep||||reg||1
Z||000002||Tim||11-18-1999||02:21 PM||||Most windshield shops have two prices for glass. If you call for a price they will give you the insurance price.  If you walk in and explain this is out of your pocket they may have a cash price.  Compare this with the cost of used glass and an installation kit that may leak.  I was quoted $306 a couple years ago, I told them too much out of my pocket.  I paid $98.00.  It took them one day to order the glass.||||reg||1
Z||000003||batboy||11-18-1999||03:56 PM||||He's right, they always charge the insurance companies the maximum. The Blazer that is assigned to me at work got a cracked in the windshield. I was told by my boss to call around and get a half dozen estimates. When I called the shops and told them I was getting quotes from several places, they all dropped their prices a whole bunch trying to get our business. I used that same method on my own personal Suburban last spring and got a great deal. It works, try it.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Patrick||11-18-1999||04:02 PM||||<BR>I've just got to pass on my Fiero windshield story...<P>I had owned my Fiero for about four months and was busy working all the bugs out of it. (There were a few... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">) Anyway, I had just got burned with a Photo Radar ticket and I decided to get a radar detector. (I drove my Z28 for <B>eight years</B> and never got a ticket. Now with 1/3 the horsepower, I get a ticket...) I was inside the Fiero and I was pushing the suction-cup detector mount onto the top of the inside of the windshield, <B>and the whole damn windshield tipped right up out of the frame!</B> I couldn't believe it, there was NOTHING holding the windshield in place other than gravity! The weirdest thing is, the windshield did NOT leak. And it rains here, let me tell you. I know how important the windshield is for the structural integrity of any car, so I immediately got it fixed, but I wouldn't have believed what I had experienced unless I had seen it with my own eyes.||||reg||4
Z||000005||88 Fiero||11-18-1999||04:26 PM||||There is a company that sells a lense cover that you could install in front of your license plate in which it will blurr out your license plate number in a certain angle...for laser radar...your best bet will be paint the car in black and block out as much refective lense as possible...this is the reason why I switch with a PISA taillight....black color will absorb the laser beam and it will not bounce back to the police laser gun...If you have a bright color car...expect that to reflect back...Oh yeah...I read that on an old article of Car and Driver....||||reg||1
Z||000006||Racer 1||11-18-1999||04:44 PM||||Just paint your car with carbon fiber resin paint. Like whats on the F-117 stealth aircraft that stuff. Then nothing will see you. I got my windsheild for around $140.00 but that had the tinting on top the window without tinting is cheaper.||||reg||1
Z||000007||DISenchanted||11-18-1999||05:25 PM||||Patrick,<BR>I have the same problem with my windshield.  It's just sitting there.  I need to know what type of sealant I should use.  I also assume I need a new piece of rubber striping.  Any Ideas where to aquire it?<P>Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000008||88 Fiero||11-18-1999||05:54 PM||||You can buy the Rubber Stripping from the Fiero Store...||||reg||1
Z||000009||Patrick||11-18-1999||06:35 PM||||<BR><B>88 Fiero</B>, my Fiero is black, but those license plate covers are illegal here in BC.<P><B>DISenchanted</B>, I can't answer your question, but...<P>When I discovered my loose windshield, I went to a shop to have it set and sealed in properly. The owner of the shop asked me if I had windshield replacement as part of my auto insurance. I just shrugged because I hadn't even thought of my car insurance for this repair. He pointed out a small ding in the windshield just above my sight line and said that it would warrant repair by my insurance company. He also pointed out that because the ding was in the tinted portion of the windshield, that "invisible" repair of the glass could not be done without it showing up. Therefore the whole windshield would have to be replaced. I went to the insurance claim centre and had them look at it. My claim was accepted and they gave me my paperwork. I was pleased to see that the deductable was only $50, but to my horror they had put down for an "invisible" repair. Well, that was no good. My windshield would still not be held in properly. I went back to the desk and explained about the ding being in the tinted portion of the glass, etc. The woman gave me a pained look and snapped that the deductable would be $100 to replace the windshield. She probably expected me to forget about it, but little did she know that I was actually quite pleased. The $100 was probably cheaper than if I simply had the old, dinged windshield remounted as I had originally planned. And I now have a nice new windshield. <P>Anybody reading between the lines here can gleam a lot of useful information. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>PS. Now that I've thought about it a little more, it's possible that there was NO deductable for the "invisible" repair, and a $50 deductable for having the windshield replaced. I don't remember, but it seems to me that there was a $50 difference somewhere. This was about 2 1/2 years ago, and I'm getting old and forgetful. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Patrick (edited 11-18-1999).]||||reg||14
Z||000010||batboy||11-18-1999||08:09 PM||||According to "The Big Fiero Parts Book" the windshield and rear glass is bonded in place by a polyurethane sealer. A specific procedure is used that requires special cleaning, using a urethane primer, and a mandatory curing time at a specific temperature. They conclude that you should have a qualified auto glass shop install the Fiero windshield and rear glass.||||reg||1
Z||000011||SCCA FIERO||11-19-1999||12:03 AM||||My 86SE was coming out of storage to get back on the road after 5 years of hybernating. The windshield had a crack in it that would not pass inspection, so I called around and found the best price at $116.00 installed. That was at noon on a Monday. I took it to get the inspection done then off to stand in line at the DMV for 2 hours. I gave them my 50 bucks for licensing, ran outside and slapped the 99 sticker over the 93 sticker and took off. <P>The next day at noon I was driving to lunch and down the 2 lane road came a dumptruck with dirt and crud following behind it. It flew past me with a gust that almost blew me off the road. Then I heard a <B>CRACK</B> yep...it cracked my 24 hour old windshield right in the center. It spread about 5 inches within an hour then sprung a few cracks in the other direction. My luck...<P>EDIT:  I mispelled storage<p>[This message has been edited by SCCA FIERO (edited 11-19-1999).]||||reg||1
Z||000012||Linx||11-19-1999||11:26 PM||||I drove around with a crack this long for almost two years.  Some gal i know that's "in the business" suggested that my comprehensive policy might cover it.<P>Some time later, while I was droppin' off my payment, I remembered what my gal friend said- and asked the agent.  She told me that my deductable was a whoppin' $500.  She pointed out that for another $12, she could write a zero deductable.  Cool.  Catch was, she'd have to look the car over for damage.  She hopped up from her seat and went out to the lot...walked around the car twice <I>and never noticed the crack!</I><P>Two weeks later, Im at a traffic light, waiting for the green and I noticed a glass shop across the road.  What the heck! I popped in- they called my agent, and an hour later I was sporting new glass!<P>Ive since thought it over and decided that there was no way that sweet gal could have overlooked that crack...it was as big as my ex-wife.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  I think she let me slide.||||reg||1
